  "description": "Two experimental states of air in an inverted flask with its neck immersed in water: heating expels bubbles; cooling draws water into the neck. Apparatus is schematic and carries no numerical scale.",
  "source": {
    "image": {"path": "ssot-resources/soviet10year-textbooks/artifacts/6p/figures/fig-11.png", "sha256": "08275b0554a6cdfe72cd12309527a93546b66868bbea554815331938c63276e2"},
    "authoritativeText": [{"lesson": "phy6-c2-s2", "text": "图 11 所示的是一个玻璃烧瓶，瓶颈浸在水中。当对烧瓶加热时，空气就把水从瓶颈中排出，并开始有气泡往外冒，这表明空气受热时体积增大了（图 11，a）。而当烧瓶冷却时，水就进入瓶内，这表明留在瓶内的空气的体积减小了（图 11，b）。"}],
    "inventory": [
      {"id": "heated-state", "description": "Source left panel: sloping immersed neck, round flask bulb, water basin, spirit burner and heat under bulb, three bubbles near the immersed outlet, label a. No scale values. Water hatching and flask contours are modern schematic regularizations, not new measured facts.", "objects": ["basin-a", "water-a", "flask-a", "burner-a", "heat-a", "bubble-a1", "bubble-a2", "bubble-a3", "label-a"], "assertions": ["bubble-count", "label-count", "bubble-1-in-water", "bubble-2-in-water", "bubble-3-in-basin"]},
